  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1800.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1806.08 CDL Waiver for Certain Military Applicants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1806.08 CDL Waiver for Certain Military Applicants.\n\n(a) Notwithstanding any other rule to the contrary, the road skill examination set forth above, shall be waived if the applicant completes and submits a “Test Waiver Military Application (DSMV 609)”, (Rev. 09/2024).\n\n(b) Applicants submitting form DSMV 609 shall sign and date the form, and in doing so, shall certify under the penalties of perjury that the information on the form is true and correct to the best of the applicant’s knowledge, information, and belief.\n\n(c) The applicant submitting form DSMV 609 shall also obtain their commanding officer’s certification of the applicant’s commercial driving experience on form DSMV 609.\n\n(d) The commanding officer shall sign and date form DSMV 609, and in doing so, shall certify under the penalties of unsworn falsification, pursuant to RSA 641:3, that the applicant named in part 1 is or was assigned in a job or assignment requiring operation of a commercial motor vehicle that the information the commanding officer provided is correct.\n\n(e) If all requirements in (a) through (d) are satisfied, military applicants from the following military occupational specialties or occupation classifications shall be eligible for a knowledge test waiver if the most recent experience with the vehicle type for which the waiver is being sought occurred within the last year:\n\n(1) U.S. Army:\n\na. 88M – Motor Transport Operator;\n\nb. 92F – Fueler; or\n\nc. 14T – Patriot Launching Station Operator;\n\n(2) U.S. Marine Corps, 3531 – Motor Vehicle Operator;\n\n(3) U.S. Navy, EO – Equipment Operator; or\n\n(4) U.S. Air Force:\n\na. 2T1 – Vehicle Operator;\n\nb. 2F0 – Fueler; or\n\nc. 3E2 – Pavement and Construction Equipment Operator.\n\nSource. #10523, eff 2-18-14, EXPIRED: 2-18-24\n\nNew. #13963, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-13-24; ss by #14100, eff 10-18-24, EXPIRES: 10-18-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1800.html"
}
